{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/399135-2e-raise-the-familiar-questions","id":399135,"title":"[2E] Raise the Familiar questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T12:09:52-08:00","id":399135,"title":"[2E] Raise the Familiar questions","content":"Simple ones that the book doesn't elaborate on:<br /> <br /> Does the Familiar get an effect Blood Potency score, and therefore the ability to carry Vitae?<br /> <br /> Can it spend the Vitae it has like a ghouled animal could?<br /> <br /> The book says that it can't hunt for itself or turn blood into Vitae, but could a Vampire who wasn't its creator feed it, or could its creator command it to take blood from another Kindred? Basically, can it obtain Vitae from a source other than its creator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:48:24-08:00","id":399241,"title":"","content":"I would treat it as two separate &quot;templates&quot; added to an animal. Using Raise the Familiar does not allow it to carry vitae, use disciplines, or anything related to ghouldom. However, using RtF also doesn't stop you from ghouling the familiar either. <br /> <br /> So, the animal, if ghoul, would be able to obtain vitae from other vampires. Otherwise, not. The only thing that RtF would absolutely require is using the power ever few days to keep it alive, which needs vampire to spend the blood as part of using the discipline; the rest follows normal ghoul rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:53:48-08:00","id":402669,"title":"","content":"I don't think so, but I would consider it BP 0 if it matters for some other purpose.<br /> <br /> Nope. You might be able to get away with ghouling it.<br /> <br /> The vampire that feeds has a special connection so that would be problematic, but if you hand wave it off as long as the Vitae is given on behalf of the one that raised the familiar then I don't see a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T12:17:03-08:00","id":406008,"title":"","content":"RtF only works on dead animals, so you can't really have both templates on the same animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>